<title>ESTONIA: NOON RADIO HEADLINES - MARCH 25.</title>
<headline>NOON RADIO HEADLINES - MARCH 25.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>These were the headlines on Estonian Kuku radio at noon. Reuters has not verified these reports and does not vouch for their accuracy:</p>
<p>-15,000 Estonian schools students start writing their end-of-year school exams today.</p>
<p>-Danish intellengence experts say Russia is delaying Baltic border agreements to keep them out of NATO.</p>
<p>-Culture Minister Jaak Allik sees the need for local Russian language television station to better integrate Russians into Estonia's society.</p>
<p>--Tallinn newsroom +372 630 8400 reuters@reuters.ee</p>
